# The cases of the copies under tests/tables/ that do not agree with nuc, read by tests/tables.rs
# (TEST-template-table-cases): '<table> | <case name> | <rule> | <status>' a line, the table without
# '.txt', the status 'pending <ticket>', the ticket under docs/plan/ that ports the case, 'not
# ported <reason>', for a rule nuc leaves to the bash (ARCH-rules-need-only-git), or 'decided by
# <ADR> <reason>', for a case an ADR in force decides otherwise for nuc.

check-devcontainer | a Dev Container without VS Code, where the host-side clause binds nothing | devcontainer/check | decided by API-command-line-with-measure — nuc writes only findings on the standard output, so its pass is the exit 0 and a summary on the standard error, and no line ends in the bash's key of a passing check
check-devcontainer | a brace or bracket in an entry before the git settings | devcontainer/check | decided by API-command-line-with-measure — nuc writes only findings on the standard output, so its pass is the exit 0 and a summary on the standard error, and no line ends in the bash's key of a passing check
check-devcontainer | a container without a socket, pinned and locked, passes | devcontainer/check | decided by API-command-line-with-measure — nuc writes only findings on the standard output, so its pass is the exit 0 and a summary on the standard error, and no line ends in the bash's key of a passing check
check-devcontainer | a mount whose target comes last, under another of its names | devcontainer/check | decided by API-command-line-with-measure — nuc writes only findings on the standard output, so its pass is the exit 0 and a summary on the standard error, and no line ends in the bash's key of a passing check
check-devcontainer | a project mounted under a path of its own | devcontainer/check | decided by API-command-line-with-measure — nuc writes only findings on the standard output, so its pass is the exit 0 and a summary on the standard error, and no line ends in the bash's key of a passing check
check-devcontainer | a project without a Dev Container or VS Code settings | devcontainer/check | decided by API-command-line-with-measure — nuc writes only findings on the standard output, so its pass is the exit 0 and a summary on the standard error, and no line ends in the bash's key of a passing check
check-devcontainer | a project without a Dev Container | devcontainer/check | decided by API-command-line-with-measure — nuc writes only findings on the standard output, so its pass is the exit 0 and a summary on the standard error, and no line ends in the bash's key of a passing check
check-devcontainer | an engine inside the container talks to no host engine and is the project's choice | devcontainer/check | decided by API-command-line-with-measure — nuc writes only findings on the standard output, so its pass is the exit 0 and a summary on the standard error, and no line ends in the bash's key of a passing check
check-devcontainer | the git settings in a postStartCommand string pass | devcontainer/check | decided by API-command-line-with-measure — nuc writes only findings on the standard output, so its pass is the exit 0 and a summary on the standard error, and no line ends in the bash's key of a passing check
check-devcontainer | the nuc Feature on another major tag | devcontainer/check | decided by API-command-line-with-measure — nuc writes only findings on the standard output, so its pass is the exit 0 and a summary on the standard error, and no line ends in the bash's key of a passing check
check-docs-record | a base without the release line counts as none | docs/template-release | decided by API-version-coupling-hook-defaults — it checks the tree as the v0.1.0 its README names, a release before this check
check-docs-record | a change that moves the release line while a NUC- ADR is proposed | docs/template-release | decided by API-version-coupling-hook-defaults — it checks the tree as the v0.2.0 its README names, a release before this check
check-docs-record | a release line that says 'not forked' | docs/base-blobs | decided by API-version-coupling-hook-defaults — it checks the tree as the v0.8.1 its README names, a release without this check
check-docs-record | no README to carry the Template release line | docs/template-release | decided by API-version-coupling-hook-defaults — it refuses a tree without a README before any rule runs
check-docs-record | the first release cut while a NUC- ADR is proposed | docs/template-release | decided by API-version-coupling-hook-defaults — it checks the tree as the v0.1.0 its README names, a release before this check
check-shell | a project's script that calls no enter_root | shell/root | not ported under ARCH-rules-need-only-git, since it runs the project's scripts
check-shell | a quoted case label with an alternative reads a value | shell/root | not ported under ARCH-rules-need-only-git, since it runs the project's scripts
check-shell | a script whose enter_root is its own reads a missing root | shell/root | not ported under ARCH-rules-need-only-git, since it runs the project's scripts
check-shell | a script without rest_args, which takes --verbose | shell/root | not ported under ARCH-rules-need-only-git, since it runs the project's scripts
check-shell | a self-test whose floor does not stop it | shell/bash-floor | not ported under ARCH-rules-need-only-git, since it runs the project's scripts
check-shell | a skill script whose floor does not stop it | shell/bash-floor | not ported under ARCH-rules-need-only-git, since it runs the project's scripts
check-shell | an option a test reads a value after, written without one in the usage | shell/root | not ported under ARCH-rules-need-only-git, since it runs the project's scripts
check-shell | an option whose branch reads a value, written without one in the usage | shell/root | not ported under ARCH-rules-need-only-git, since it runs the project's scripts
